          <h2>Matchday traffic around Villa Park</h2>
          <p>Erdington sits close to <a href="birmingham.html">Birmingham</a> city centre, and when there's a match on at Villa Park, the volume of traffic in and around the area increases sharply, and car parks and side streets fill up fast. A breakdown at these times is more disruptive than usual, both for you and for other vehicles trying to get in or out, so if your car won't move after a game, let us know it's a matchday — we'll factor the extra traffic into how we plan getting to you and clearing the vehicle.</p>

          <h2>Retail park recovery</h2>
          <p>Erdington has a significant concentration of retail parks, including the Fort Shopping Park, and a fair share of our call-outs here happen in supermarket or retail car parks — flat batteries after a short shopping trip, or a car that won't start after sitting for a while. These sites are usually straightforward for us to reach, but multi-level car parks or busy weekend car parks can still need some care, so tell us which store or unit you're nearest to.</p>

          <h2>Where two roads meet</h2>
          <p>Erdington sits at a genuine junction point in Birmingham's road network. The A38(M) Aston Expressway runs down from Spaghetti Junction on the M6 towards the city centre, and the M6 itself passes close by via the Gravelly Hill interchange. If you've broken down on either of these roads rather than in a car park, your direction of travel and the nearest junction or landmark help us get to you as directly as possible.</p>

          <div class="callout">
            <p><strong>Broken down after a match at Villa Park?</strong> If you can, wait somewhere well clear of the exit routes other vehicles are using — a quiet corner of the car park rather than blocking a lane. Call us with the venue and roughly which car park you're in, and we'll work around the matchday traffic.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

